We are doing Q2W2 Monday: Agree on the first task. I use a Mac and ChatGPT in a browser; I will copy your files into VS Code myself. Use the attached current source snapshot. At the start of this week: Only the existing README and Git history exist. The actual snapshot takes precedence if a prior repair changed the file layout.

Today's request: Our repository contains only README.md. Draft docs/product-brief.md, docs/board.md, and docs/prompt-log.md. The finished product needs manual rooms/classes/teacher scheduling, conflict checks, Microsoft sign-in with Admin and Teacher roles, publishing, Azure teaching deployment, and a permanent VPS by Q4W8. Exclude student enrollment. Put all future features in Backlog. Put only a React page with a heading and purpose sentence in Ready. Include an acceptance check. Do not generate app code or replace README.md.

Use these current file locations where they apply: README.md; docs/product-brief.md; docs/board.md; docs/prompt-log.md; frontend/package.json; frontend/index.html; frontend/src/main.jsx; frontend/src/App.jsx; .gitignore. Create only files needed for today's task. Preserve existing paths unless a specific change is necessary. Return complete contents for each changed file, one labeled code block per path, and Mac run/test commands with working directories. Use VS Code GUI actions for Git operations. Do not use placeholders for facts already in the snapshot. If an account-specific value is missing, ask for that value before generating dependent configuration.

