4. Click Publish Branch for the first upload and choose origin if asked. If already published, click Source Control > … > Push. Confirm the branch is lesson/q2w2-tue and wait for the upload to finish.
5. Press Command+Shift+P and select GitHub Pull Requests: Create Pull Request. Set the base to the actual default branch and compare to lesson/q2w2-tue. Enter the lesson title and observed check results, then click Create.
6. Open Changes in Pull Request and review each diff with a student. In the PR Description, confirm required checks and approvals, then use the available Merge action and confirm. If blocked, keep the PR a draft/unmerged. If nothing changed, skip the empty commit and PR.
7. After GitHub confirms Merged, exit Review Mode if it is active. Click the bottom-left branch picker and select the default branch.
8. Click Source Control > … > Fetch, then … > Pull. Confirm the merged files appear in Explorer and there are no uncommitted changes or unexpected outgoing commits. Leave this updated default branch ready for the next lesson.
The next lesson begins from this merged checkpoint. If branch protection requires another approved reviewer, complete that review before proceeding. Do not force-push to bypass it.
