4 Send the complete lesson prompt
We are doing Q2W8 Tuesday: Build the manual planner. I use a Mac and ChatGPT in a browser; I will copy your files into VS Code myself. Use the attached current source snapshot. At the start of this week: Rooms and catalog records exist; there are no meetings or planner. The actual snapshot takes precedence if a prior repair changed the file layout.

Today's request: Build only a manual draft planner for the existing Meeting API. Use course/section, room, weekday, and period selectors with clear labels. Show saved meetings ordered by weekday and numeric period. Include empty and error states. No drag-and-drop, automatic placement, student enrollment, sign-in, or hidden future controls. Keep existing catalog screens.

Use these current file locations where they apply: backend/models.py, backend/main.py, backend/schemas.py, backend/alembic/versions/; frontend/src/App.jsx and planner components. Create only files needed for today's task. Preserve existing paths unless a specific change is necessary. Return complete contents for each changed file, one labeled code block per path, and Mac run/test commands with working directories. Use VS Code GUI actions for Git operations. Do not use placeholders for facts already in the snapshot. If an account-specific value is missing, ask for that value before generating dependent configuration.

Our acceptance check is: Section A appears at Monday P1 in Room 101 after reload; the list order follows days and periods. Explain the expected observation and one relevant failure case. Do not report a pass until I provide actual output. Do not implement any later week's feature.

Use the supplied manual checks today. If the request above mentions tests, provide manual expected/actual cases only; the automated pytest framework is introduced in Q3W1.
5 Review then save each file
Send this review request in the same chat before copying the proposed code:
Review the file contents you just proposed against today's exact task and the attached current source. Name every affected path. Check imports, dependencies, commands, preserved behavior, and any unrelated or future-feature code. Give a corrected complete file only if needed; otherwise say no correction is needed. Identify which checks I must run on my Mac. Do not say they passed yet.
For each returned path, use VS Code Explorer. Create any missing parent folder with New Folder, then New File. For an existing file, open that exact file, select all its text with Command+A, paste the complete replacement, and save with Command+S. Copy only the code-block contents, not the surrounding backticks or explanation. Compare the changed paths with today’s task; reject unrelated future features.
