If students use approved accounts on separate computers, their PR targets lesson/q2w8-tue until that class branch is merged. First, the teacher saves, reviews, stages, and clicks Commit, then Publish Branch (or … > Push). Students use Source Control > … > Fetch and the branch picker to open that published class branch; if already on it, use … > Pull. Students must receive today’s reviewed files before editing.
After the student contribution, repeat the visible acceptance check and run these commands before committing:
npm --prefix frontend run build
8 Record and save the reviewed result
In the same ChatGPT chat, paste a short factual observation: what you did, what appeared, and the actual build/test result. Then paste this request. Save the note as docs/lesson-notes/Q2W8-Tue.md and the revised board at its existing path.
Write docs/lesson-notes/Q2W8-Tue.md for Q2W8 Tuesday, task Build the manual planner. Use only the observations I have just supplied to write today's lesson note. Include the task, the prompt improvement students made, paths changed, expected and actual results, pass/fail/not run, and the student contribution. Do not invent a successful check. Also provide the smallest change to docs/board.md that moves only verified work to Done; keep failures Blocked with a next action. Return complete contents for the named lesson-note file and revised board. Do not change application code.
In VS Code choose File > Save All. Click Source Control, then each file under Changes to inspect its diff. Click the + beside only each intended source, document, migration, or lockfile. Keep .env, virtual environments, node_modules, dist, dumps, and tokens out of Staged Changes. Then complete these steps:
1. In Source Control, click each file under Staged Changes to review the exact saved changes. If you edit again, save and stage that file again.
2. In the Message box, enter: Q2W8 Tuesday Build the manual planner
3. Click Commit. If asked to stage everything, cancel and stage only the intended files with +.
4. Click Publish Branch for the first upload and choose origin if asked. If already published, click Source Control > … > Push. Confirm the branch is lesson/q2w8-tue and wait for the upload to finish.
5. Press Command+Shift+P and select GitHub Pull Requests: Create Pull Request. Set the base to the actual default branch and compare to lesson/q2w8-tue. Enter the lesson title and observed check results, then click Create.
6. Open Changes in Pull Request and review each diff with a student. In the PR Description, confirm required checks and approvals, then use the available Merge action and confirm. If blocked, keep the PR a draft/unmerged. If nothing changed, skip the empty commit and PR.
7. After GitHub confirms Merged, exit Review Mode if it is active. Click the bottom-left branch picker and select the default branch.
8. Click Source Control > … > Fetch, then … > Pull. Confirm the merged files appear in Explorer and there are no uncommitted changes or unexpected outgoing commits. Leave this updated default branch ready for the next lesson.
The next lesson begins from this merged checkpoint. If branch protection requires another approved reviewer, complete that review before proceeding. Do not force-push to bypass it.
