Create an isolated PostgreSQL test target
From the repository root, create scheduler_test. If it already exists, confirm that it is the disposable test database before running tests. Never point tests at scheduler or a hosted database.
docker compose up -d db
docker compose exec db createdb -U scheduler scheduler_test
The main prompt will make the test fixture derive the test URL from the local DATABASE_URL and enforce the scheduler_test database name. It must refuse class/production targets. Save the generated tests before using the commands printed after the file-saving step.
