Today's request: Protect concurrent scheduling writes in the current one-active-term app. In one transaction acquire SELECT FOR UPDATE on the existing Term row before reading fresh relevant meetings/sections/rooms, then validate and write. Apply the same boundary to every scheduling-affecting create/update/delete path. Preserve foreign keys and appropriate uniqueness constraints. At READ COMMITTED, read after acquiring the lock rather than reusing stale ORM state. Add a real two-request PostgreSQL race test; mocks or SQLite do not establish this behavior.

