4 Send the complete lesson prompt
We are doing Q4W5 Monday: Fix the top observed failure. I use a Mac and ChatGPT in a browser; I will copy your files into VS Code myself. Use the attached current source snapshot. At the start of this week: User acceptance has produced a prioritized list of real findings. The actual snapshot takes precedence if a prior repair changed the file layout.

Today's request: Here is our highest-priority reproducible issue, expected result, actual result, current files, and failing check. Propose and apply the smallest correction to that issue only. Preserve all required workflows and explain changed lines. Include a regression test that would fail before this repair. If the supplied evidence does not show a defect, ask for a specific diagnostic instead of inventing one.

Use these current file locations where they apply: only the files implicated by the observed defect and its regression test; existing manifests for justified dependency updates. Create only files needed for today's task. Preserve existing paths unless a specific change is necessary. Return complete contents for each changed file, one labeled code block per path, and Mac run/test commands with working directories. Use VS Code GUI actions for Git operations. Do not use placeholders for facts already in the snapshot. If an account-specific value is missing, ask for that value before generating dependent configuration.

Our acceptance check is: The original failure is resolved and nearby regression checks pass with evidence linked to the issue. Explain the expected observation and one relevant failure case. Do not report a pass until I provide actual output. Do not implement any later week's feature.
5 Review then save each file
Send this review request in the same chat before copying the proposed code:
Review the file contents you just proposed against today's exact task and the attached current source. Name every affected path. Check imports, dependencies, commands, preserved behavior, and any unrelated or future-feature code. Give a corrected complete file only if needed; otherwise say no correction is needed. Identify which checks I must run on my Mac. Do not say they passed yet.
For each returned path, use VS Code Explorer. Create any missing parent folder with New Folder, then New File. For an existing file, open that exact file, select all its text with Command+A, paste the complete replacement, and save with Command+S. Copy only the code-block contents, not the surrounding backticks or explanation. Compare the changed paths with today’s task; reject unrelated future features.
6 Run the check and handle a failure here
1. Repeat the selected failure before repair, then repeat it after repair and run nearby passing cases.
