The check failed. The actual command, expected result, observed result, and first error are pasted immediately above. Use today's source snapshot and the files we changed in this chat. Identify the failing layer and give one small diagnostic first. Then give the smallest correction, complete contents for any changed file, and the exact Mac recheck command. Preserve working data and unrelated behavior. Do not regenerate the entire app or implement future tasks.
Save only the correction it returns, rerun the failed check, and repeat relevant earlier checks. If no failure occurred, skip the repair prompt. Keep the aide’s paper exercise moving while the teacher diagnoses.
