4 Send the complete lesson prompt
We are doing Q4W8 Monday: Complete the final acceptance record. I use a Mac and ChatGPT in a browser; I will copy your files into VS Code myself. Use the attached current source snapshot. At the start of this week: The finished candidate and operating guides are ready for final verification. The actual snapshot takes precedence if a prior repair changed the file layout.

Today's request: Prepare the final acceptance record from the real evidence I provide. Cover all agreed product requirements and the permanent VPS. Include Azure teaching deployment evidence, role/conflict/publication checks, persistence, and operational ownership. Mark any failed or untested required item as incomplete and identify an immediate repair/retest task. Never turn a required failure into a deferred refinement.

Use these current file locations where they apply: docs/final-acceptance.md, docs/release-notes.md, docs/handoff.md and docs/board.md; keep the accepted VPS release running. Create only files needed for today's task. Preserve existing paths unless a specific change is necessary. Return complete contents for each changed file, one labeled code block per path, and Mac run/test commands with working directories. Use VS Code GUI actions for Git operations. Do not use placeholders for facts already in the snapshot. If an account-specific value is missing, ask for that value before generating dependent configuration.

Our acceptance check is: Every required row is a supported pass by Q4W8; otherwise the record accurately states incomplete and class time stays on repair. Explain the expected observation and one relevant failure case. Do not report a pass until I provide actual output. Do not implement any later week's feature.
5 Review then save each file
Send this review request in the same chat before copying the proposed code:
Review the file contents you just proposed against today's exact task and the attached current source. Name every affected path. Check imports, dependencies, commands, preserved behavior, and any unrelated or future-feature code. Give a corrected complete file only if needed; otherwise say no correction is needed. Identify which checks I must run on my Mac. Do not say they passed yet.
For each returned path, use VS Code Explorer. Create any missing parent folder with New Folder, then New File. For an existing file, open that exact file, select all its text with Command+A, paste the complete replacement, and save with Command+S. Copy only the code-block contents, not the surrounding backticks or explanation. Compare the changed paths with today’s task; reject unrelated future features.
6 Run the check and handle a failure here
1. Run every required final check on VPS and verify the recorded Azure evidence. Resolve any required failure before signing completion.
In a separate repository-root terminal, run the checks below. Run only against the isolated local test configuration when pytest is included. A stopped service or missing dependency must be resolved before recording a pass.
npm --prefix frontend run build
cd backend
.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
cd ..
If a check fails: copy the exact command, the first useful error, what you expected, and what appeared into the same ChatGPT chat. Remove credentials. Then paste this ready-to-use repair request:
The check failed. The actual command, expected result, observed result, and first error are pasted immediately above. Use today's source snapshot and the files we changed in this chat. Identify the failing layer and give one small diagnostic first. Then give the smallest correction, complete contents for any changed file, and the exact Mac recheck command. Preserve working data and unrelated behavior. Do not regenerate the entire app or implement future tasks.
Save only the correction it returns, rerun the failed check, and repeat relevant earlier checks. If no failure occurred, skip the repair prompt. Keep the aide’s paper exercise moving while the teacher diagnoses.
7 Guide the student contribution
Students independently verify one assigned browser outcome and compare their result with a peer.
Use the aide-supervised classroom Mac for the reference workflow so students do not need a separate advanced environment. Rotate driver and reviewer. The driver makes only the approved small edit or writes the evidence note; the reviewer compares the diff and runs the supplied check. Record each student’s name/pseudonym and contribution in docs/student-work/. The teacher controls account authentication and the final push.
If students use approved accounts on separate computers, their PR targets lesson/q4w8-mon until that class branch is merged. First, the teacher saves, reviews, stages, and clicks Commit, then Publish Branch (or … > Push). Students use Source Control > … > Fetch and the branch picker to open that published class branch; if already on it, use … > Pull. Students must receive today’s reviewed files before editing.
After the student contribution, repeat the visible acceptance check and run these commands before committing:
npm --prefix frontend run build
cd backend
.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
cd ..
